{"id":"xKHHTwjQLrC7","title":"Dune","copyright":1965,"description":"On the desert planet Arrakis, the most valuable substance in the universe is found beneath the sands, and control of it is the prize in a ruthless game of empire. Young Paul Atreides, heir to a noble house betrayed and brought low, emerges from that ruin into a destiny no one could have predicted. The desert people called the Fremen see in him the figure of their prophecies, the one known as Muad'dib, who will avenge his family and reshape the fate of humanity itself. Herbert's epic braids together political intrigue, ecological vision, mysticism, and hard-edged adventure into a story that has anchored science fiction's imagination for generations.","subtitle":"Book One in the Dune Chronicles","type":"fiction","createdAt":"2026-08-22T07:53:21Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-22T07:53:21Z","genres":[{"id":"NF493Q9ygkpm","title":"Action \u0026 Adventure"},{"id":"J8RQmxkzcMFV","title":"Fantasy"},{"id":"4pnwAczyaHXx","title":"Science Fiction"}],"images":[{"id":"DPWg4eiXd6xV","url":"https://cdn.audiobookdb.org/5cf545b54ebd37e5db8629c13c630aa18c25dcbc1d8a003677da341488ea1044","sourceUrl":"https://cdn.audiobookdb.org/5cf545b54ebd37e5db8629c13c630aa18c25dcbc1d8a003677da341488ea1044/source.jpg:book","width":2400,"height":2400,"blurdata":"UnJ~f0n%9ws.=^odNIWW0$WqkBWVIra#kAfj"}],"coverImage":{"id":"DPWg4eiXd6xV","url":"https://cdn.audiobookdb.org/5cf545b54ebd37e5db8629c13c630aa18c25dcbc1d8a003677da341488ea1044","sourceUrl":"https://cdn.audiobookdb.org/5cf545b54ebd37e5db8629c13c630aa18c25dcbc1d8a003677da341488ea1044/source.jpg:book","width":2400,"height":2400,"blurdata":"UnJ~f0n%9ws.=^odNIWW0$WqkBWVIra#kAfj"},"originalLanguage":{"name":"English"},"people":[{"role":{"name":"Author"},"person":{"id":"7zjxPdJg6feY","name":"Frank Herbert","description":"Frank Herbert was born in Tacoma, Washington, in 1920. Before establishing himself as a full-time writer, he spent his early career working as a reporter and later as an editor for several West Coast newspapers. His first science fiction story appeared in print in 1952, though widespread recognition came more than a decade later. That breakthrough arrived through the pages of *Analog* magazine, which serialized his two-part tale \"Dune World\" and \"The Prophet of Dune.\" Herbert combined the two installments into the novel *Dune*, published in 1965, the work that brought him lasting fame. He continued writing until his death in 1986.","roles":[{"role":{"name":"Author"},"book":{"id":"mBBNgm3prbar","title":"Angels' Fall","images":[{"id":"gTtLXmBER83j","url":"https://cdn.audiobookdb.org/d84d650c81d1cd2dc336970eea0ffd6874839bc0309821a9de90b45ac22a543d","sourceUrl":"https://cdn.audiobookdb.org/d84d650c81d1cd2dc336970eea0ffd6874839bc0309821a9de90b45ac22a543d/source.jpg:book","width":2400,"height":2400,"blurdata":"UMB{-[t604M|?GofM{RR~9oe9cR*tOWXnjnj"}]}},{"role":{"name":"Author"},"book":{"id":"AjfeniFKVUwU","title":"The Green Brain","images":[{"id":"aRYBnMUVhGK7","url":"https://cdn.audiobookdb.org/9c8c862ca2e47c51ba9e1208451912840c198af020d9fa4a3e92a3fac8f38fb1","sourceUrl":"https://cdn.audiobookdb.org/9c8c862ca2e47c51ba9e1208451912840c198af020d9fa4a3e92a3fac8f38fb1/source.jpg:book","width":2560,"height":2560,"blurdata":"UOFXuMMvNFo}=tRjt7t5_}xwWFV@E,xuROV]"}]}},{"role":{"name":"Author"},"book":{"id":"tQb7fPBzf4RE","title":"The Eyes of Heisenberg","images":[{"id":"8BRR3JH4UyT9","url":"https://cdn.audiobookdb.org/3803f9aabf90305645ad355f1f66ececefbd8f3b37430f300dac678a4fdee6b5","sourceUrl":"https://cdn.audiobookdb.org/3803f9aabf90305645ad355f1f66ececefbd8f3b37430f300dac678a4fdee6b5/source.jpg:book","width":2560,"height":2560,"blurdata":"U77-{oS,M_t7toWAaes+EFr.nyf--,tTbeby"}]}},{"role":{"name":"Author"},"book":{"id":"ie89xUFUWwar","title":"Man of Two Worlds","images":[{"id":"n9xRFWkrdTiT","url":"https://cdn.audiobookdb.org/9ebc21241fd54302ba0df6d3bb6ba2b2d3bca7dae4bfac1ea1de4c395888b44b","sourceUrl":"https://cdn.audiobookdb.org/9ebc21241fd5430